; multiplicative compiler-correctness bridge: the product of a tree's leaves = the product over its flattened list. evalP e = product(flatten e).
; evalP folds (*) over the Expr AST (Leaf v->v, Node l r-> evalP l * evalP r); flatten lists the leaves. By tree induction: Leaf v -> product[v]=v*1=v (n*1=n); Node -> product distributes over append [product-append] and the two IHs close it. Completes the flatten value-bridges: eval<->sum (additive) and evalP<->product (multiplicative), both showing flatten carries a commutative-monoid tree fold to the matching list fold.
